          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "きがかり — kigakari — \"a worry; something on one's mind\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "もし あめが ふったら、ははは こどもの ことが きがかりでしょう。 — moshi ame ga futtara, haha wa kodomo no koto ga kigakari deshō — \"If it rains, my mother will be worried about the children.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A na-adjective: な before a noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "きがかり (kigakari) mixes the two layers, native and Sino-Japanese: Sino-Japanese ki, \"spirit\" (Middle Chinese khj+jH), borrowed from Chinese, and native gakari, \"hanging\", the voiced form of kakari, from kakaru, \"to hang\" (JMdict, KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
